rom private actors whose primary incentive is to secure market dominance. Instead, governments must enforce rigorous 'compute-audits' and capability-based licensing to ensure that no system exceeds human-controllable limits without verified safety guarantees. This is not about stifling innovation; it is about ensuring that innovation does not result in the permanent obsolescence of human oversight. Effective policy requires enforceable, transparent, and international standards that prioritize global stability over local competitive advantage. 🛡️",
